      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you're describing a slow, quiet erosion of your life, which is often just as devastating as a sudden tragedy because there's no one to blame or rush to fix. This numbness you feel is actually your mind's way of protecting you from the crushing weight of having everything you loved drain away over time. You don't need to feel sad right now; you just need to feel the relief of finally letting go of the impossible expectation that things should have stayed the same.",
